{"text": " You wake up in 1882 in Lower Manhattan. It's the 4th of September, a Monday afternoon. Horses, newspapers, the clatter of the street. Did you know that when Thomas Edison's lights came on, he wasn't at the power station? He was standing in the office of the banker JP Morgan. Here's your afternoon. At about three o'clock, an engineer on Pearl Street closes a switch, a few blocks of office's light up, about 400 lamps and not one of them has a flame. The glowing bulb was the easy part. Edison sold the rest, generators, copper under the street, meters and investors willing to bet a fortune on it. What does one hour of light cost you now? By 1900, about 13 minutes of work. So what is light now? A network. You plug into a system you'll never see, but that bulb turns most of its power into heat. The fix takes more than 100 years, and one color nobody can make.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 2.06, "text": " You wake up in 1882 in Lower Manhattan.", "tokens": [50364, 509, 6634, 493, 294, 2443, 32848, 294, 25523, 23633, 13, 50488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12576693347376636, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 0.014098168350756168, "words": [{"word": " You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.14, "probability": 0.8868004083633423}, {"word": " wake", "start": 0.14, "end": 0.3, "probability": 0.9781419634819031}, {"word": " up", "start": 0.3, "end": 0.48, "probability": 0.9991700649261475}, {"word": " in", "start": 0.48, "end": 0.6, "probability": 0.9962635636329651}, {"word": " 1882", "start": 0.6, "end": 1.36, "probability": 0.9944911301136017}, {"word": " in", "start": 1.36, "end": 1.66, "probability": 0.854653537273407}, {"word": " Lower", "start": 1.66, "end": 1.76, "probability": 0.8333491683006287}, {"word": " Manhattan.", "start": 1.76, "end": 2.06, "probability": 0.9973740577697754}]}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 2.56, "end": 5.36, "text": " It's the 4th of September, a Monday afternoon.", "tokens": [50488, 467, 311, 264,